      {
        "day_number": 11,
        "title": "When Hope Feels Closed",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Romans 3:23-24; Revelation 21:27.</p><p><strong>Story context:</strong> The first mission-room sermon focuses on the purity and peace of the heavenly city.</p><p><strong>Source-based editorial paraphrase:</strong> Christie listens with longing, but he hears the exclusion of sin more clearly than the promise of mercy. At home he repeats the fearful part to Treffy, who concludes that he has no hope. The two remain distressed because the story of grace has not yet reached them fully.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> A true message can be badly misunderstood when heard only in fragments. The holiness of God must not be separated from the good news of grace through Jesus Christ.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Have you spoken about sin without making room for Christ's mercy? Consider how to communicate the whole message with care.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Gracious Father, make our words truthful and complete. Let those burdened by guilt hear the hope you give in Jesus. Amen.</p>",
