        "day_number": 12,
        "title": "The Promise of Cleansing",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> 1 John 1:7-9; Romans 5:8.</p><p><strong>Story context:</strong> In the next mission-room meeting, Mr. Wilton explains forgiveness through the death of Jesus Christ.</p><p><strong>Source-based editorial paraphrase:</strong> Christie eagerly listens as the clergyman speaks of God's mercy reaching every kind of wrongdoing. The boy realizes that the message addresses both him and Treffy. He leaves with renewed hope and the desire to share it immediately.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> Christian forgiveness is grounded in Christ's self-giving love, not in a person's age, record, or ability to earn a new beginning. Confession is a turn toward mercy rather than a purchase of it.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Where are you treating forgiveness as something to deserve? Confess honestly and receive God's invitation to begin again.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord Jesus Christ, thank you for your saving love. Teach us repentance, trust, and gratitude for your mercy. Amen.</p>",
