        "day_number": 13,
        "title": "A Prayer in the Attic",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Matthew 11:28-30; 1 John 1:9.</p><p><strong>Story context:</strong> Christie returns from the mission-room and shares what he has learned with Treffy.</p><p><strong>Source-based editorial paraphrase:</strong> The boy repeats the promise that Christ can cleanse from sin. Treffy worries that his past is too heavy, but Christie reminds him that the promise does not exclude him. Side by side in their small room, they pray in simple words for forgiveness.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> People need not possess elegant religious language before turning to God. Prayer may be honest, plain, and shared with someone who offers encouragement instead of judgment.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Could you pray with someone without correcting their words or requiring them to hide their questions?</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Merciful Jesus, receive our imperfect prayers. Help us trust your grace and accompany one another with gentleness. Amen.</p>",
