        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Colossians 1:12-14; Galatians 5:22-25.</p><p><strong>Story context:</strong> At another mission-room service, Mr. Wilton speaks of the life that follows forgiveness.</p><p><strong>Source-based editorial paraphrase:</strong> Christie hears that believers are not only welcomed by grace but also shaped over time by God's Spirit. The preacher describes the slow work of learning to love what is good and resist wrongdoing, and Christie hopes to explain this teaching to Treffy.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> Sanctification is a continuing work of the Holy Spirit, not instant moral perfection. Its fruit is seen in patient love, truthfulness, self-control, and service.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> What small habit needs the Spirit's renewing work? Choose one concrete act of patience, honesty, or kindness.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Holy Spirit, renew my desires and habits. Grow in me the fruit of a life formed by Jesus Christ. Amen.</p>",
