        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> John 14:27; John 11:25-26.</p><p><strong>Story context:</strong> The story's farewell scene follows a visit from Mr. Wilton, who comforts Christie and Treffy.</p><p><strong>Source-based editorial paraphrase:</strong> The clergyman reads Jesus' promise of peace and gently prays with the distressed boy. During the night, Treffy asks Christie to play their cherished tune. Treffy dies as the old organ sounds, leaving Christie grieving and alone.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> Christian hope in the risen Lord does not erase the pain of death or make separation desirable. The living need comfort, care, and companionship as they mourn.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> What can you do for someone newly bereaved in the days after others have gone home? Offer a specific, lasting kindness.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Risen Christ, be close to those saying goodbye and those left behind. Give them comfort and people who remain with them. Amen.</p>",
