        "title": "Returning with Good News",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Isaiah 58:6-7; 2 Corinthians 1:3-4.</p><p><strong>Story context:</strong> Years later, the fictional Christie is an adult Scripture-reader serving people in the neighborhood of his childhood.</p><p><strong>Source-based editorial paraphrase:</strong> Christie returns to Ivy Court alongside Mabel, now Mrs. Villiers. They visit a sick woman in Treffy's former attic, pray with her, and read from the small Testament once carried by Mabel's mother. Their visit joins spiritual encouragement to continuing personal attention.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> The memory of care becomes a calling to care for others. Christian service remains incomplete if it offers words but neglects food, safe housing, health, and dignity.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> How can past kindness shape the way you share Scripture and respond to someone's actual circumstances today?</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of comfort, let mercy received become mercy practiced. Join our witness to justice, generosity, and steady friendship. Amen.</p>",
