      {
        "day_number": 27,
        "title": "Love Made Visible Over Years",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> 1 John 3:18; Colossians 3:12-14.</p><p><strong>Story context:</strong> Christie's adult work takes him through the same streets and households where he once struggled.</p><p><strong>Source-based editorial paraphrase:</strong> Mrs. White remembers giving him scraps of food as a child and now speaks gratefully of his visits and care. Christie continues reading Scripture and speaking with families. At home, he is surprised by the sound of Treffy's organ and discovers that Mr. Wilton has returned to visit.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> A life of service grows through repeated, ordinary acts. The memories of old neighbors show how relationships can mature when love is offered over many years.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> What long-term relationship deserves renewed attention? Commit to a reliable action rather than a one-time display.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord Jesus, make my kindness consistent. Teach me to honor old friends and serve new neighbors with patience. Amen.</p>",
