        "title": "Faithful Work Has Limits",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Mark 14:8; 1 Corinthians 3:6-7.</p><p><strong>Story context:</strong> In their reunion, Christie and Mr. Wilton speak about the needs of the neighborhood and the work of ministry.</p><p><strong>Source-based editorial paraphrase:</strong> Christie keeps the organ in memory of Treffy. He wishes to spend more years serving because there is so much need around him. Mr. Wilton reminds him that no single person can accomplish everything and prays for faithful service within human limits.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> Service is not measured by solving every problem. We offer what we can, welcome others' contributions, and trust God with what lies beyond our control.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Where are you carrying responsibility that belongs to a wider community? Identify one task to share or one needed boundary.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord of the harvest, keep me faithful without pride or exhaustion. Help us work together and leave results in your care. Amen.</p>",
