      {
        "day_number": 26,
        "title": "Make Room for Someone’s Gifts",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> 1 Peter 4:10-11; Romans 12:4-8</p><p><strong>Source and historical context:</strong> Ranney befriends a musician whose drinking has disrupted his life and who begins contributing music to mission gatherings. He also describes meeting an employed father after a street meeting and trying to help him reconsider his choices.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> A person is more than the struggle currently visible. Skill, memory, creativity, and hope can remain present through hardship. Helping someone recover a place to contribute can be as important as meeting immediate needs. But a helper must not turn another person into a success story on demand; patient support respects their agency and circumstances.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Whose talents have I stopped noticing because I focus only on their difficulties?</p><p><strong>Practice:</strong> Invite someone to share a skill or interest in a safe, respectful setting. Listen to what kind of support they want before proposing a solution.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Creator God, help me see the gifts in every person and make room for them to flourish. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "1 Peter 4:10-11",
          "Romans 12:4-8"
        ]
