    "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/6757",
    "days": [
      {
        "day_number": 1,
        "title": "Notice What Could Help",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Proverbs 20:11; Philippians 2:4.</p><p><strong>Story and historical context:</strong> In Selina Bunbury's nineteenth-century tale The Little Pavior, Francis sees that his grandfather has slipped on a muddy path. The story presents a child whose careful attention leads him to imagine a practical repair.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> Love pays attention. Age does not prevent a person from noticing danger, understanding another person's need, and offering a thoughtful response.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> What repeated difficulty affects someone near you? Before acting, ask what would truly help and whether you need guidance, permission, or another person's skill.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of wisdom, open my eyes to the needs around me. Give me compassion, good judgment, and readiness to help. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "Proverbs 20:11",
          "Philippians 2:4"
        ]
      },
      {
        "day_number": 2,
        "title": "Work Carefully and Safely",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Colossians 3:23-24; Proverbs 22:3.</p><p><strong>Story and historical context:</strong> Francis gathers sand and stones and builds a small raised pavement. The original story celebrates his independent effort; contemporary readers should also recognize that children need safe tasks, suitable tools, and adult supervision.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> Faithful service joins diligence with wisdom. Good intentions do not remove the need to consider safety, learn from others, and complete work with care.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Is there a helpful task you have rushed or attempted without enough knowledge? Identify the next careful step and the person whose advice could make the work safer and better.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, teach me to serve wholeheartedly and wisely. Protect those who work, and help me value care above praise or speed. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "Colossians 3:23-24",
          "Proverbs 22:3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "day_number": 3,
        "title": "Let Gratitude Become Blessing",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> 1 Thessalonians 5:11; Psalm 90:17.</p><p><strong>Story and historical context:</strong> Francis's grandfather discovers the repaired path and responds with gratitude and a prayer for the child's future. The tale ends by connecting practical love with encouragement and blessing.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> When another person serves faithfully, gratitude can strengthen that person rather than merely reward an achievement. We recognize the good, thank God, and speak words that encourage continued growth.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Whose quiet effort has made your path easier? Thank the person specifically and ask God to establish the good work of their hands.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Gracious God, thank you for people whose care makes life safer and kinder. Teach me to notice their work and encourage them well. Amen.</p>",
