        "day_number": 4,
        "title": "Refuse Hasty Suspicion",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> James 1:19; 1 Corinthians 13:7.</p><p><strong>Story and historical context:</strong> In The Silver Knife, a household searches for Mary's missing knife. Several characters quickly suspect a poor child, a servant, or even a bird before they have reliable evidence.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> Love does not turn uncertainty into accusation. Christians listen carefully, resist prejudice, and seek truth without treating social status or a troubled expression as proof of guilt.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> When have you filled a gap in your knowledge with a negative story about someone? Separate what you know from what you assume, and seek the truth with patience.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of truth, slow my anger and guard my speech. Free me from prejudice and teach me to listen before I judge. Amen.</p>",
