        "day_number": 5,
        "title": "Tell the Truth and Make Repair",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Ephesians 4:25; Galatians 6:1.</p><p><strong>Story and historical context:</strong> The knife is found in a cheese, exposing a servant's false explanation and misuse of household food. Bunbury's tale ends with confession, correction, mercy, and the family's refusal to shame her through gossip.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> Truth and mercy belong together. Wrongdoing should be named and repaired, while restoration should be gentle, accountable, and protected from humiliating spectacle.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Do you need to correct a false statement, return something, or repair trust? Take responsibility plainly, and if another person confesses, respond without cruelty or gossip.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Merciful God, give me courage to tell the truth and repair harm. Make me gentle and wise when another person needs restoration. Amen.</p>",
