        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Acts 9:36-39; James 2:15-17.</p><p><strong>Story and historical context:</strong> Neighbors remember Amelia teaching, sewing clothes, visiting sick people, and helping families find work. The tale compares her with Tabitha, also called Dorcas, whose loving deeds were remembered by her community.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> Living faith addresses bodies, minds, relationships, and spiritual needs. Practical care may involve making, teaching, visiting, connecting, advocating, or sharing resources.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Which gift or ordinary skill could become care for someone else? Ask what is needed and offer that gift in a way that respects the person's choices and dignity.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord Jesus, make my faith active in love. Use my hands, knowledge, time, and relationships to serve people with dignity. Amen.</p>",
