        "day_number": 8,
        "title": "Grieve with Resurrection Hope",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> John 11:33-36; 1 Thessalonians 4:13-14.</p><p><strong>Story and historical context:</strong> Amelia's neighbors speak at her grave about the help they received from her. The narrator expresses confidence about Amelia's final state in language typical of a memorial tale; this reading leaves final judgment with God.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> Christian hope makes room for tears. We remember visible fruits with gratitude while entrusting the person who died to the just and merciful God revealed in the death and resurrection of Jesus.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Is there someone you need to remember with both honesty and gratitude? Name the loss, give thanks for specific good, and bring what you cannot know into God's care.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Risen Lord Jesus, comfort those who mourn. Receive our gratitude and questions, and anchor our hope in your resurrection. Amen.</p>",
