        "day_number": 9,
        "title": "Continue the Work of Love",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Hebrews 10:24; 2 Timothy 2:2.</p><p><strong>Story and historical context:</strong> After hearing how Amelia served, Anna and her brother record the names of people she had visited and begin helping them. Her example becomes an invitation to sustained community care rather than admiration alone.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> A faithful example bears fruit when others learn, share responsibility, and continue good work. Christian service should grow through communities instead of depending on one admired person.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> What valuable work is too dependent on one person? Consider how you can learn the task, support the worker, or help build a team that can continue serving faithfully.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of steadfast love, turn admiration into participation. Help us share knowledge, responsibility, and encouragement as we serve together. Amen.</p>",
