        "day_number": 10,
        "title": "Let Scripture Interrupt Your Path",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Psalm 119:105; Hebrews 4:12.</p><p><strong>Story and historical context:</strong> In The Tract Found by the Way-Side, Mark finds a small religious pamphlet while planning to disobey his father. He begins reading out of boredom, but the story inside challenges the direction of his life.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> God can use Scripture to interrupt settled habits and expose a better path. The power belongs to God's living word, not to a particular format or method of distribution.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> When did a biblical truth last interrupt your plans or assumptions? Return to that passage and identify the response it asks of you now.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Speaking God, shine your light on my path. Give me humility to hear your word and courage to change direction. Amen.</p>",
