        "day_number": 12,
        "title": "Encourage Change Without Control",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> 1 Thessalonians 5:11; 2 Timothy 2:24-25.</p><p><strong>Story and historical context:</strong> Mark's sister Josephine listens, answers his questions, and encourages his desire to change. Other family members begin examining their own conduct instead of treating Mark as the only problem.</p><p><strong>Devotional focus:</strong> Lasting change cannot be forced through ridicule or control. We speak truth gently, encourage the next faithful step, and remain willing to repent of the patterns we contribute to a family or community.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Are you trying to change someone through pressure, or supporting the person's own responsible choices? Adjust your words so they combine truth, patience, and respect.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Patient Lord, make my words truthful and gentle. Help me encourage growth without controlling others, and show me where I also need to change. Amen.</p>",
