        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“Who has blessed us with all spiritual blessings.”</em></p>\n<p>Ephesians 1:3</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Holiness is life being reshaped by communion with God. It appears in integrity, compassion, self-control, justice, and love rather than contempt for people who struggle or confidence in our own superiority.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Holy God, conform me to Christ and make my words, habits, and relationships bear the fruit of your love. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“Come, my beloved, let us go forth into the field ... let us see if the vine flourish.”</em></p>\n<p>Song of Solomon 7:11,12</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> Creation is God's good gift, entrusted to human care rather than exploitation. Receive its beauty with gratitude, respect the limits of creatures and ecosystems, and practice stewardship that serves future neighbors too.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Creator of heaven and earth, awaken gratitude and teach me to care faithfully for the world and its creatures. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "Ephesians 1:3",
          "Song of Solomon 7:11,12"
        ]
      },
      {
        "day_number": 131,
        "title": "May 10",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“But now is Christ risen from the dead.”</em></p>\n<p>1 Corinthians 15:20</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Christian hope rests in the bodily resurrection of Jesus and God's promise to raise the dead and renew creation. This hope does not silence grief; it gives courage to remain faithful within it.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Risen Christ, meet me in grief and hope, and form in me a life that bears witness to your resurrection. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“The only begotten of the Father, full of grace and truth.”</em></p>\n<p>John 1:14</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> God's mercy is gift, not payment for achievement or respectability. Receive grace without self-contempt, extend it without favoritism, and remember that forgiveness never makes another person's suffering unimportant.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Merciful God, let your grace free me from shame and pride, and make me generous in forgiveness, truth, and repair. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "1 Corinthians 15:20",
          "John 1:14"
        ]
      },
      {
        "day_number": 132,
        "title": "May 11",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“I am with you always.”</em></p>\n<p>Matthew 28:20</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> This verse directs our attention to Jesus Christ, the eternal Son who became truly human for our salvation. Receive what it reveals about his character or work, and let trust in him take visible form in love.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord Jesus Christ, true God and true human, draw me into your life and teach me to follow you in love. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“Only be you strong and very courageous.”</em></p>\n<p>Joshua 1:7</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> Faith is not denial of evidence, pain, or honest questions. It is a growing reliance on God's character that can seek wisdom, receive help, and take the next faithful step without pretending certainty we do not have.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Trustworthy God, hold me amid uncertainty and guide my next step in wisdom, courage, and love. Amen.</p>",
