        "day_number": 224,
        "title": "August 11",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“Oh that I were as in months past.”</em></p>\n<p>Job 29:2</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> This verse meets human fear, grief, illness, or weakness without turning suffering into proof of guilt. Trust in God can coexist with lament, safety planning, medical care, counseling, and the support of a faithful community.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Compassionate God, stay near in suffering, lead me toward wise help, and make me attentive to another person's pain. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“Everlasting consolation.”</em></p>\n<p>2 Thessalonians 2:16</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> Holiness is life being reshaped by communion with God. It appears in integrity, compassion, self-control, justice, and love rather than contempt for people who struggle or confidence in our own superiority.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Holy God, conform me to Christ and make my words, habits, and relationships bear the fruit of your love. Amen.</p>",
