        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“Accepted in the beloved.”</em></p>\n<p>Ephesians 1:6</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Holiness is life being reshaped by communion with God. It appears in integrity, compassion, self-control, justice, and love rather than contempt for people who struggle or confidence in our own superiority.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Holy God, conform me to Christ and make my words, habits, and relationships bear the fruit of your love. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“Jesus said to him, If you can believe.”</em></p>\n<p>Mark 9:23</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> This verse directs our attention to Jesus Christ, the eternal Son who became truly human for our salvation. Receive what it reveals about his character or work, and let trust in him take visible form in love.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord Jesus Christ, true God and true human, draw me into your life and teach me to follow you in love. Amen.</p>",
