        "day_number": 5,
        "title": "Peacemaking Beyond Pride",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Matthew 5:9; James 3:17-18</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> Burt condemned a contemporary war among Christian-majority countries. In the middle of a national sermon, he questioned pride and revenge dressed as patriotism.</p><p><strong>Source-based editorial paraphrase:</strong> Burt asks that love of country turn away from pride and revenge toward concern for other people.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Jesus calls peacemakers blessed. Peacemaking begins where we resist dehumanizing speech and listen before taking a side. It also seeks justice for those harmed. Where could you replace pride or retaliation with a truthful, peace-seeking action?</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Prince of Peace, turn our anger away from cruelty. Teach me to seek justice and peace with humility, courage, and love. Amen.</p>",
