        "title": "Serve the Common Good",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Jeremiah 29:7; Matthew 5:16</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> The original conclusion also treats America's future as specially bound to national Christian identity. This reading draws its call to integrity into a prayer for the good of all who share a community.</p><p><strong>Source-based editorial paraphrase:</strong> Burt closes by urging citizens to resist corrupt party loyalties and seek fair representation. He links the nation's welfare to the moral choices of its people.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Jeremiah urged exiles to seek the welfare of the city where they lived. Honest public life serves people across parties and beliefs. What local need could you meet with a neighbor this week? Choose a step that helps without asking for recognition.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, help me seek the good of my community. Give its leaders integrity and give me a generous heart toward every neighbor. Amen.</p>",
