        "day_number": 6,
        "title": "Christ Remains",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Philippians 2:12-13; Hebrews 13:8.</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> After Storr's death, Hoare asked how the congregation should continue without its longtime pastor. He directed them beyond the absent leader to the continuing presence and work of Jesus.</p><p><strong>Source theme, in contemporary language:</strong> Trusted leaders may leave, retire, or die, but Jesus Christ remains. Christian maturity receives help from teachers while depending on God, who continues to work within his people.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Has a change in leadership unsettled your faith or community? Name what you have lost, then identify one practice that keeps your attention on Christ and strengthens others.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Unchanging Lord Jesus, hold your people through every transition. Work in us, keep us close to you, and help us serve one another faithfully. Amen.</p>",
