        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> John 10:41-42; 2 Corinthians 4:5.</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> May connected Storr's ministry with the Gospel's description of John the Baptist: John performed no sign, yet his testimony about Jesus proved true. The memorial's claims about Storr are treated here as local testimony.</p><p><strong>Source theme, in contemporary language:</strong> Christian witness does not need spectacle or personal greatness. Its task is to speak truthfully about Jesus and help people trust him, while admitting the witness's own limits and faults.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Do your words about faith direct attention toward Jesus or toward your own image? Choose one simple and honest way to testify to Christ through speech or service.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord Jesus, keep my witness honest and centered on you. Use ordinary words and actions to help others see your truth and mercy. Amen.</p>",
