        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Matthew 6:6; Psalm 1:1-3.</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> The notes from Storr's final sermon turn from the memorial to John the Baptist. They describe hidden preparation through prayer, self-examination, Scripture, and communion with God before public ministry.</p><p><strong>Source theme, in contemporary language:</strong> Visible faithfulness grows from hidden roots. Private prayer and sustained attention to Scripture prepare believers for public responsibility without making spiritual discipline a performance.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Which hidden practice would deepen your roots: unhurried prayer, Scripture meditation, confession, or silence? Set a realistic time and place to begin.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, meet me in the quiet place. Root me in your word and form a life that bears good fruit in its season. Amen.</p>",
