        "title": "Pray and Work for the Common Good",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> 1 Timothy 2:1-2; Micah 6:8.</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> Hopkins closed an official civic sermon by calling rulers and citizens to responsibility before God. This reading retains the call to prayer and integrity without treating one nation or political system as God's kingdom.</p><p><strong>Source theme, in contemporary language:</strong> Christians can pray for public leaders, seek peaceful conditions, practice justice, and walk humbly with God. Political outcomes never replace the church's hope in Jesus Christ.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Name one leader or public concern that usually produces anger or anxiety in you. Pray specifically, then identify one peaceful and truthful action that serves your neighbor.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, give wisdom to those who hold public responsibility. Make us people of justice, mercy, humility, and peace, with our lasting hope in Jesus Christ. Amen.</p>",
