    "description": "Nineteen Scripture-led devotional readings inspired by M. W. Mayow’s 1867 lecture, published in 1868, on the first report of the Royal Commission on Ritual and the Book of Common Prayer. Explore faithful worship, conscience, Christian freedom, fair church decisions, leadership, respectful disagreement, inherited tradition, and hope for unity. The readings place his Anglican ceremonial and legal arguments in their historical context rather than treating them as binding rules for all Christians. Each day offers Scripture, source context, reflection, a practical response, and prayer.",
