        "day_number": 1,
        "title": "Every Believer Can Strengthen Others",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Hebrews 13:7; 1 Peter 4:10.</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> Herbert James preached after the 1864 funeral of John Pemberton Plumptre. He used one local Christian life as an example, while directing praise to God's grace rather than to the deceased.</p><p><strong>Source theme, in contemporary language:</strong> God gives gifts to the church for the good of others. A believer may serve through words, example, hospitality, work, or quiet faithfulness; no act of service is too small to matter.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Think of one gift, skill, or opportunity God has entrusted to you. Who could be strengthened if you used it with humility today?</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of grace, help me use what you have given me for the good of others and the honor of Jesus Christ. Amen.</p>",
