        "title": "Prayer Nourishes Faith",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Philippians 4:6-7; Hebrews 11:6.</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> The first sermon connects sustained faith with private prayer and regular attention to Scripture. Its local memories support a wider invitation to seek God faithfully.</p><p><strong>Source theme, in contemporary language:</strong> Faith needs nourishment. Scripture directs the mind toward God's promises, and prayer brings duties, disappointments, cares, and fears into God's presence.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Which concern keeps circling in your thoughts? Turn it into a specific prayer, and choose a short passage of Scripture to revisit during the day.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Faithful God, meet me in Scripture and prayer. Guard my heart with your peace and strengthen me to trust you in what I cannot control. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
