        "day_number": 4,
        "title": "Humility and Love Take Action",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Philippians 2:3-5; 1 John 3:18.</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> James remembered humility and practical love as prominent features of Plumptre's life. The sermon says these qualities came from the grace of Christ rather than personal importance.</p><p><strong>Source theme, in contemporary language:</strong> Humility makes room for Christ to be seen, and love becomes real through action. Christian care attends to both bodily needs and spiritual encouragement.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Whose needs are easy for you to overlook? Choose one concrete act of care that protects the person's dignity and expects no recognition.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Jesus, form your humility in me. Let my love move beyond kind intentions into patient and practical service. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
