        "day_number": 5,
        "title": "Let Your Life Bear Good Fruit",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Matthew 5:16; Philippians 2:15-16.</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> At the close of the first sermon, James urged his hearers to live faithfully in the places where God had set them. The appeal is separated here from the details of the funeral.</p><p><strong>Source theme, in contemporary language:</strong> A faithful life can leave neighbors stronger, comforted, and more attentive to Christ. Good works do not earn salvation; they bear witness to the grace already received.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> If someone observed your ordinary week, where might they see the light of Christ? What habit of selfishness, delay, or indifference needs to change?</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, make my ordinary work fruitful. Help me hold firmly to your word and serve in a way that directs gratitude to you. Amen.</p>",
