      {
        "day_number": 6,
        "title": "Follow the Lamb",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Revelation 14:4-5; John 10:27.</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> Edward Hoare's second sermon begins with the symbolic vision in Revelation 14. He applies it to faithful discipleship; this reading avoids the sermon's nineteenth-century sectarian controversy.</p><p><strong>Source theme, in contemporary language:</strong> Those who belong to Jesus listen for his voice and follow him. Faithfulness includes truthfulness, wholehearted devotion, and refusal to join what draws the heart away from Christ.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Where are you tempted to follow approval, habit, or fear instead of Jesus? Identify one step of truthful obedience you can take today.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lamb of God, keep me near your voice. Give me an undivided heart and make my words truthful and gracious. Amen.</p>",
