        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> 1 Peter 1:18-19; Revelation 5:9.</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> Hoare emphasizes redemption through Jesus while interpreting the funeral text. This devotion retains the Christ-centered confession without repeating the sermon's polemical comparisons.</p><p><strong>Source theme, in contemporary language:</strong> Jesus gave himself to redeem people for God. His saving work calls believers away from empty ways of life and into grateful worship, holiness, and love.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> What pattern feels empty but familiar? Bring it honestly to Christ, and ask how gratitude for his saving love could reshape your next choice.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord Jesus, thank you for giving yourself for us. Turn me from empty habits and form in me a life of worship, holiness, and love. Amen.</p>",
