        "title": "Grace Produces Honest Witness",
        "content": "<p><strong>Read:</strong> Ephesians 2:8-10; Colossians 3:9-10.</p><p><strong>Historical context:</strong> The second sermon closes by joining grace, truthful character, and service. Its claims about the deceased are treated as local testimony rather than a guarantee about any person's final state.</p><p><strong>Source theme, in contemporary language:</strong> Salvation is God's gift, and the new life it creates is marked by truth and good work. Honest Christian witness neither hides sin nor pretends that moral effort replaces grace.</p><p><strong>Reflect:</strong> Is there a place where your words and actions do not agree? Ask God for courage to tell the truth, repair harm, and practice the good work prepared for you.</p><p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of truth and grace, renew me in Christ. Make my speech honest, my repentance sincere, and my service useful to others. Amen.</p>",
